      "writtenOn": "2025-10-06T23:51:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you really think we need a new timeout, or simply reuse lock_timeout? The corner case is that if uses did not specify lock_timeout, which the default is 5000, and they will get a delayed lock timeout error.\n\nDigging into it, there are only two cases:\n\n- other contains_revision(): as you mentioned this is a read step and should finish instantly, so 20s or 5000s does not make a lot of differences. Only for cases that one process is hanging, the error will be raised late. Does it happen a lot? For such case, I think we should figure out the hanging, as a shorter timeout does not help resolve the hanging issue, right?\n- other gclient sync: lock_timeout is WAI.",
      "parentUuid": "0204929f_3bca6cd7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3971,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 3971,
